{
  "$comment": [
    "What scripts/site-crops.mjs cuts out of the captures, and how. Run it with --sources <folder>.",
    "rect: [x, y, width, height] in the capture's CSS pixels (scale: capture pixels per CSS pixel),",
    "or { \"ref\": \"path/in/the/rects/index\" } with optional pad and x/y/w/h overrides.",
    "widths: the files written, img/<name>-<width>.avif and .webp; the page's srcset follows them.",
    "fade: CSS pixels over which an edge the crop cuts through fades to that edge's own colour."
  ],
  "scale": 2,
  "rects": "rects.json",
  "out": ".",
  "href": "img/",
  "page": "../index.html",
  "formats": {
    "avif": { "quality": 62, "speed": 4 },
    "webp": { "quality": 82, "method": 6 }
  },
